<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">10 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 10 September, from 506 to 1939.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">506</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bishops of Visigothic Gaul meet at the Council of Agde</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">With the permission of the Arian king Alaric II, Catholic bishops met at Agde and issued canons on clerical discipline, marriage and church property. Many entered later collections of church law.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1419</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John the Fearless is murdered on the bridge at Montereau</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Duke of Burgundy was killed by followers of the Dauphin Charles during peace talks. Burgundy allied with England, leading to the Treaty of Troyes that made Henry V heir to France.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1813</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Oliver Hazard Perry wins the Battle of Lake Erie</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Perry's American squadron captured the entire British force on Lake Erie. His message 'We have met the enemy and they are ours' heralded the recovery of Detroit and the American north-west.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1846</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Elias Howe patents the lockstitch sewing machine</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Elias Howe received a US patent for a machine using an eye-pointed needle and a shuttle to form a lockstitch. He later won royalties from Singer and other makers who used his design.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1939</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Canada declares war on Germany</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A week after Britain, Canada's parliament declared war on Germany in its own right. More than a million Canadians served in the Second World War.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a></div></li></ol>
